flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Complete the following checks: 1. Inspect the<br/>protective window and lens for spatter pitting or<br/>residue. 2. Check the beam path enclosure for damage<br/>or contamination ingress. 3. Inspect the lens<br/>mounting ring for looseness or mechanical damage."]
    box_2{"Lens or beam path window scratched, chipped or<br/>contaminated?"}
    box_3(["End, Replace optics: lens or window damage detected,<br/>station offline"])
    box_4["With the laser shut off, blow dry compressed air at<br/>the protective window from the clean side to remove<br/>loose debris. Apply one drop of optical cleaning<br/>fluid to a lint free applicator and wipe the inner<br/>surface using a single stroke in one direction.<br/>Inspect the window under a torch at oblique<br/>incidence; replace the window if spatter pitting or<br/>scratch damage covers more than 10% of the clear<br/>aperture."]
    box_5["Access the laser head cooling circuit status display<br/>or read the thermal sensor value from the laser<br/>controller diagnostic menu. Record the coolant inlet<br/>and outlet temperatures at the laser head block. A<br/>difference greater than 5 degrees Celsius between<br/>inlet and outlet at idle indicates a flow<br/>restriction; compare both values against the rated<br/>operating temperature range in the laser system<br/>specification."]
    box_6[/"Refer to the laser head thermal operating limits."/]
    box_7{"Laser head temperature within rated operating range?"}
    box_8(["End, Escalate: laser head overtemperature, check<br/>chiller circuit"])
    box_9["Insert a sheet of thermal paper at the nominal focal<br/>plane with no workpiece present. Fire a single low<br/>power alignment pulse and inspect the burn mark<br/>position and shape. The burn mark should be centred<br/>within 0.5 millimetres of the nominal beam centre<br/>reference point marked on the alignment jig. An<br/>elliptical burn pattern indicates astigmatism or a<br/>tilted beam delivery optic."]
    box_10[/"Refer to the beam alignment specification."/]
    box_11{"Beam centred within 0.1 mm of field centre?"}
    box_12["Adjust beam steering mirror, tilt and pan micro<br/>adjusters"]
    box_13{"Reverify beam alignment after mirror adjustment"}
    box_14(["End, Escalate: beam misalignment unrecoverable,<br/>optical bench check"])
    box_15["Connect a calibrated photodetector power meter to<br/>the laser beam path using the external power<br/>measurement tap or by directing the beam at the<br/>detector through the standard safety aperture.<br/>Command the laser to its nominal output power<br/>setting and record the measured power. Compare the<br/>reading against the power specification tolerance<br/>and investigate if the reading is more than 5% below<br/>the specification floor."]
    box_16[/"Refer to the laser power output specification."/]
    box_17{"Output power within ±5% of rated value at 100% duty<br/>cycle?"}
    box_18["Complete the following steps: 1. Navigate to the<br/>laser power calibration menu in the marking<br/>software. 2. Place the calibrated power meter at the<br/>focal plane and follow the on-screen sequence. 3.<br/>Record the measured output power and confirm it<br/>meets the specification."]
    box_19{"Reverify output power after calibration routine"}
    box_20(["End, Escalate: laser power unrecoverable, source<br/>degradation suspected"])
    box_21["Connect an oscilloscope to the Q switch trigger<br/>signal output at the laser controller. Command the<br/>laser to the standard pulse frequency used for the<br/>production marking program. Measure the period<br/>between successive trigger pulses and calculate the<br/>actual frequency. Compare against the programmed<br/>frequency and confirm the deviation is within 0.5%<br/>of the commanded value."]
    box_22[/"Refer to the laser pulse frequency specification."/]
    box_23{"Pulse frequency stable at all programmed values?"}
    box_24["Inspect Q switch driver board connections and clean<br/>circuit board"]
    box_25["Mount the graduated focal test sample in the marking<br/>fixture at the nominal standoff distance. Mark a<br/>line across the full graduation range while stepping<br/>focus in 0.5 millimetre increments per segment.<br/>Inspect the marked line under a magnifier and<br/>identify the segment with the narrowest, cleanest<br/>line width; record the corresponding focus offset<br/>and compare against the value stored in the machine<br/>setup parameter table."]
    box_26[/"Refer to the focal length specification."/]
    box_27{"Focal point at correct working distance ±0.2 mm?"}
    box_28["Adjust z axis focus offset in marking controller"]
    box_29["Hold a calibrated anemometer probe at the extraction<br/>port inlet while the extraction unit is running at<br/>the operating duty cycle. Record the air velocity in<br/>metres per second and calculate volumetric flow rate<br/>from the duct cross sectional area. Compare against<br/>the minimum extraction flow rate specified for this<br/>laser power class in the safety datasheet."]
    box_30[/"Refer to the exhaust extraction flow specification."/]
    box_31{"Extraction flow rate above minimum required value?"}
    box_32["Replace extraction filter cartridge and recheck flow"]
    box_33["Remove the scan head cover and inspect each galvo<br/>mirror surface under a torch at grazing incidence<br/>for dust, spatter deposits, or surface oxidation.<br/>Blow clean with dry compressed air through the scan<br/>head purge port. Do not touch mirror surfaces; if<br/>spatter deposits are found that cannot be cleared by<br/>air, log the condition and schedule mirror<br/>replacement at the next planned maintenance window."]
    box_34{"Galvo mirror surfaces clean and undamaged?"}
    box_35["Clean galvo mirrors using specialist mirror cleaning<br/>procedure"]
    box_36["Load the standard reference substrate into the<br/>marking fixture and run the standard test mark<br/>program. Inspect the produced marks under a<br/>reference illumination source and confirm that line<br/>width, depth, and contrast are within the limits<br/>recorded on the product mark quality standard.<br/>Document the substrate lot number and the test<br/>result in the laser log."]
    box_37[/"Refer to the test mark quality acceptance criteria."/]
    box_38{"All 10 test marks within depth, width and contrast<br/>specification?"}
    box_39["Adjust mark speed and power for substrate batch<br/>compensation"]
    box_40{"Reverify test mark quality after parameter<br/>adjustment"}
    box_41(["End, Escalate: mark quality unrecoverable, process<br/>engineering review"])
    box_42["Place the field calibration target on the work<br/>surface and run the nine point calibration routine<br/>from the laser controller software menu. The routine<br/>commands a calibration mark at each of the nine grid<br/>positions and compares the measured mark positions<br/>against the reference grid dimensions. Record the<br/>residual error at each calibration point and confirm<br/>the maximum residual is below the marking accuracy<br/>tolerance."]
    box_43[/"Refer to the field distortion tolerance."/]
    box_44{"All 9 calibration grid points within ±0.05 mm of<br/>nominal?"}
    box_45["Complete the following steps: 1. Navigate to the<br/>field distortion correction menu in the marking<br/>software. 2. Place the field calibration target on<br/>the work surface at nominal focal distance. 3. Run<br/>the correction routine and verify residual field<br/>error is within tolerance."]
    box_46["Load five consecutive production parts and run the<br/>production marking program at normal production<br/>parameters. Inspect each mark immediately after<br/>completion for completeness, position, contrast, and<br/>absence of spatter. Record the part serial numbers<br/>and the pass or fail result for each; any fail at<br/>this stage requires recalibration before production<br/>release."]
    box_47{"Production samples meet drawing marking<br/>requirements?"}
    box_48["Log all power, alignment and calibration data"]
    box_49(["End, Procedure complete"])

